[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
The if_rtwb module is not loaded automatically.  To use it instead of
the LinuxKPI rtw88 driver, add the following to /etc/rc.conf:

kld_list="${kld_list} if_rtwb"
devmatch_blocklist="if_rtw88"
wlans_rtwb0="wlan0"
create_args_wlan0="country XX"
ifconfig_wlan0="WPA DHCP"

Replace XX with your country code.  For countries whose entry in
/etc/regdomain.xml has no VHT channels (e.g. those using the APAC
regulatory domain), add "-vht" to create_args_wlan0, otherwise net80211
falls back to 11a on 5 GHz.

The adapter firmware comes from wifi-firmware-rtw88-kmod-rtw8822b.
Statistics and debugging knobs are under "sysctl dev.rtwb.0".
EOM
}
]
